kb:extraction-run-ledger
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/integrations/llm/__tests__/extractor.test.ts" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:triple-extraction ;
    pred:part-of kb:vocabulary-grounding ;
    pred:decided "RUN CONTRACT. ExtractionRun carries id, sourceId, immutable source hash/revision, pipeline version, backend and exact model, prompt/schema identifiers, selected vocabulary with selector reason, ordered stage records, start/end timestamps, terminal status, token/cache/latency metrics, output statement ids, validation counts and a failure record. Every stage is created, running, succeeded, failed or skipped; a requested provider returning no usable result is FAILED, never silently omitted from a report." ;
    pred:decided "PIPELINE ORDER. acquire normalized source -> select vocabulary/schema -> invoke provider and parse candidates -> typed shape/invariant validation -> ground evidence -> normalize identities -> compute review patch. The first deployed boundary combines invoke and parse in `extract`, then makes validation separately visible; a later split must preserve historic run readability. Stage inputs and outputs are typed and hashed, so changing one stage can be benchmarked without pretending the rest changed." ;
    pred:has-status "in-progress" ;
    pred:progress "FIRST FOUNDATION SHIPPED LOCALLY 2026-08-16. Dexie v8 adds an additive extractionRuns table indexed by id/sourceId/start/status. `ingest.svelte.ts` creates a metadata-only ExtractionRun after source hashing and records the existing configured route (including its locality and why a missing cloud key selected the pre-existing WASM fallback), then transitions route -> extract -> validate -> ground -> normalize -> archive -> diff -> persist. Source.latestExtractionRunId and each newly proposed Statement.extractionRunId link the run without storing source bytes, prompts, raw responses or keys. The existing WASM -> mock behavior is unchanged but now exposes two attempts — failed WASM then successful browser-local placeholder — instead of laundering the fallback as clean WASM success; Source records the actual placeholder extractor while the run preserves the requested WASM primary. Archive cancellation records cancelled, provider/pipeline errors record failed at the active stage and rethrow." ;
    pred:decided "STORAGE BOUNDARY. Add a dedicated IndexedDB extractionRuns table rather than growing Source into an execution log. Source points to its latest settled run; each proposed Statement carries extractionRunId. Compact run metadata and hashes may round-trip with graph provenance, while raw prompts, raw model output and source bodies remain local trace artifacts and are excluded from normal publication. Secrets are never recorded." ;
    pred:progress "FOCUSED EVIDENCE 2026-08-16: 53 extractor + ExtractionRun + ingest-archive + atomic-persist tests passed; full unit suite 146 files / 2,016 tests passed; svelte-check 0 errors (81 pre-existing warnings). The atomic-persist test injects a statement-table failure and verifies no source, statement, run or changelog durable record survives; it separately verifies an intentional policy-held zero-statement result still persists its source, terminal run and audit record. Output statement ids come from the preflight shared write funnel's accepted plan, not a requested batch or reactive-store inspection, so content-policy/archive holds do not become false persisted-output claims. A read-only local qwen3-coder review found one valid hole — a repository prompt lazy-import outside the tracked boundary could leave a run running — and it was moved inside `extract`. Its validation-slice claims of broken parser arithmetic and a Turtle bypass were checked and rejected: the parser count is `array entries - retained entries`, tested directly, and Turtle is intentionally already parsed. A later local review request returned no usable text in its time budget and is not evidence; it made no graph or source edits." ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/stores/kb.svelte.ts" ;
    pred:progress "VALIDATION SLICE 2026-08-16. `parseTriplesJSONWithReport` preserves raw-chat candidate and parser-rejected counts as metadata only; `validateExtractedTriples` rejects blank ids, invalid literal/datatype pairs, non-finite scalar literals, invalid confidence and malformed optional fields before Statement conversion. A provider with zero usable candidates now makes its run fail at `validate` before either graph write; a mixed batch proceeds with explicit losses. Direct Turtle import skips this boundary because it already has parsed statements. Claude/Ollama/WASM adapters currently return post-parser triples, so their candidate count is truthful for returned values but cannot reveal entries their private parser discarded; unifying adapter result metadata remains open." ;
    pred:constraint "OBSERVABILITY MUST NOT CREATE A SECOND PRIVACY LEAK. Recording every prompt and response by default would duplicate the most sensitive user material. Default traces retain schemas, hashes, counts, timings and failure messages; full raw traces are an explicit local debugging option with deletion controls and never sync/publish implicitly." ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/stores/ingest.svelte.ts" ;
    pred:feature-id "F136.1" ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/storage/db.ts" ;
    pred:decided "ROUTING IS RUN EVIDENCE. The run records the route policy/version, decisive signal and every provider attempt rather than only the final backend/model. Retry or escalation may recover the extraction, but it cannot erase the primary failure, hide a change in data locality or merge multiple attempts' metrics into a misleading single-call total." ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/integrations/llm/extractor.ts" ;
    pred:constraint "ATOMIC SUCCESS BOUNDARY IS IMPLEMENTED FOR INGEST ONLY. Source, accepted statements, their changelog entries and the terminal successful run now commit in one Dexie transaction after shared preflight. User-mediated archive prompts and post-commit notifications/hooks are intentionally outside it; their failure cannot relabel a committed run. Other historical callers that separately call addSource and addStatements remain outside this guarantee. Cancellation is distinct from failure, and any retry must create a new run linked to the prior one rather than rewriting history." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:work-tiering ;
    pred:relates-to kb:model-routing-ledger ;
    pred:progress "ATOMIC INGEST PERSISTENCE 2026-08-16. The shared `addStatements` admission logic is factored into `prepareStatementsForWrite`, then ingest passes its exact accepted plan to `persistIngestBatch`. One Dexie transaction writes the source, accepted statement rows, statement changelog rows and succeeded terminal ExtractionRun; reactive state, source callbacks, autosave/export, and best-effort review notification are post-commit only. The transaction deliberately still permits a source/run with zero statement rows when content/archive policy holds every candidate; an empty provider result fails earlier at validate. A late official-graph switch throws, preventing a run incorrectly marked successful with no commit. Scope is this ingest path only, not every existing addSource-plus-addStatements caller." ;
