kb:ref-exxperts
    pred:relates-to kb:capability-awareness ;
    pred:relates-to kb:design-observed-archive ;
    pred:open-question "Their memory is files with links back to conversations; ours is a graph with reified provenance. Their approach is cheaper and more portable; ours can answer questions across memories that a file cannot. Worth understanding what their file-based time travel CANNOT do before assuming the graph earns its cost — the comparison is a real test of the thesis, not a reassurance exercise." ;
    rdfs:label "exxperts (EXXETA) — local-first agent memory, approval-gated" ;
    pred:description "github.com/EXXETA/exxperts, flagged by Matt for graph-assistant continuity. TypeScript, Apache-2.0, local-first, multi-provider. Fetched 2026-07-30: persistent per-agent 'rooms'; after each session the room PROPOSES what is worth remembering and the user approves before anything enters memory; notes consolidate into long-term memory under review; every memory links back to the conversation it came from, enabling time travel to what the agent knew on a given date." ;
    pred:copy-permitted "Apache-2.0" ;
    pred:evidence "INDEPENDENT CORROBORATION OF THE GOVERNANCE SHAPE, which is why it is worth recording. It arrives at propose-then-human-approves, provenance back to source, and time-travel-to-a-past-state — the same triad as F52's agent-edit boundary, kb:passage-grounding and F97.5 — WITHOUT a knowledge graph, storing 'plain files on your machine'. Two projects reaching the same governance from different substrates is evidence the governance is load-bearing rather than an artifact of choosing RDF." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Concept> .

