    pred:principle "CONSTRAINTS BEFORE CAPABILITY; DETERMINISTIC SIGNALS BEFORE MODEL JUDGEMENT. First exclude targets that violate task capability, user egress policy, availability or hard cost/latency limits. Then use explicit task overrides and named workflow signals such as parse, schema, SHACL or grounding failure. Benchmarked policy comes next. An LLM classifier may propose a tier only when none of those can decide, and an LLM judge never certifies its own success." ;
