kb:session-2026-07-12
    pred:decision "WORK TIERING (kb:work-tiering, F74.3): route every recurring task to the cheapest tier that can do it correctly — script (rule-checkable, zero tokens, zero triage) > local agent (judgment over language, proposals only, inside a ground/prompt/validate/emit harness) > Claude Code (hardware-bound, cross-file reasoning, decides process, writes code that lands). Offloading is NOT free: a noisy local job moves cost from generation to triage. Prefer growing the SCRIPT tier. Promotion ladder: what Opus does twice becomes a job; what an agent gets right reliably becomes a script." ;
    pred:decided-on "2026-07-12"^^xsd:date ;
    pred:relates-to kb:rdf-dataset-migration ;
    pred:relates-to kb:adult-content-policy ;
    rdfs:label "Decisions — 2026-07-12 (work tiering · RDF format · safety policy)" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Decision> ;
    pred:decision "EGRESS (kb:data-egress-model): export is a RIGHT, distribution is a PRIVILEGE. Plain-text export of the user's own graph is never blocked; gates apply only where Reckons.AI is the intermediary carrying content to someone else. graph-lint enforces BOTH directions." ;
    pred:decision "SAFETY RECORD (scripts/offline/safety-attestation.ts): the app retains no identity record for graph activity or publishing, so it retains verified evidence about the SOFTWARE — a dated, hash-linked, weekly attestation that the good-faith controls exist and still pass. The hosted remote/CI history supplies timing evidence; git history alone can be rewritten, so 'cannot be backdated' is too strong. Records failures deliberately; a log that only records success is worthless as evidence. The separate F20 feedback path does not establish who authored a graph." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:work-tiering ;
    pred:decision "PUBLISHING (kb:byo-static-host, F76): never a registrar, never a host. Ease of self-hosting is a SAFETY-POLICY dependency — 'export it and self-host' is only a fair answer if self-hosting is genuinely easy." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:byo-static-host ;
    pred:relates-to kb:data-egress-model ;
    pred:decision "RDF FORMAT (kb:rdf-dataset-migration, F75): TriG in, Turtle out. Readers accept TriG (done); files stay .ttl with a default graph; .trig only when a KB genuinely carries >1 source. Grounded in kb:provenance-model — a named graph on a single-source KB is ceremony carrying zero information." ;
    pred:decision "ADULT CONTENT — OPTION C (kb:adult-content-policy, F66.1): gate only what we carry. No mediated distribution channel for adult content; authoring, storage and export unimpeded. Deletes the gameable attestation entirely — context is never an input to the gate, so there is nothing to lie about. No product accounts, graph-content backend, identity record or age-verification surface FOR THIS PATH. The F20 feedback endpoint is a separate voluntary PII path with its own notice/retention duties." ;
    pred:artifact "COUNSEL-BRIEF.md — engineering brief for Data Insight Solutions LLC's counsel: what the software sees (nothing), what it controls (best-effort, bypassable by design), the tiers, and the surviving question (does 18 U.S.C. 2258A attach to a tool that hosts nothing?)." .

