kb:ingest-routing
    pred:principle "THE DESTINATION IS A DECISION, NOT A DEFAULT. Today an ingest lands wherever the user happens to be standing, which silently makes 'the graph I last opened' the filing system. Offering a ranked destination turns an accident into a choice — but it must remain a CHOICE: the router proposes, the human disposes, because filing a fact in the wrong graph is a quiet error that compounds (it is not wrong, just unfindable)." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:open-question "What happens when NO graph scores above the threshold? Options: create a new graph named from the content (importAsNewKb already exists), fall back to the current graph, or leave the destination unset and make the user pick. Leaning: offer 'new graph' as a first-class outcome — a genuinely unrelated ingest is evidence that a new graph is wanted, and forcing it into the nearest existing one is how graphs become junk drawers." ;
    pred:depends-on kb:question-router ;
    pred:relates-to kb:multi-kb ;
    pred:relates-to kb:entity-normalization ;
    rdfs:label "Route an ingest to the most relevant graph" ;
    pred:feature-id "F103" ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:description "On the Add page, allow DESELECTING the current graph so an ingest is not implicitly filed into it, and rank the registry by how related each graph is to the extracted triples. Reuses src/lib/rdf/question-router.ts: routeQuestion() already scores candidate graphs by knows-the-subject (strongest), predicate familiarity, and neighbourhood overlap, and addressees() already thresholds so we route rather than broadcast. The generalization is the INPUT — one Question (subject + predicate, object open) becomes N extracted statements — so the work is to factor the scoring over a set of signals and call it with the ingest's subjects/predicates, NOT to write a second relevance engine." ;
    pred:constraint "REUSE routeQuestion's scoring. A parallel ingest-relevance scorer would be the fourth instance this session of the duplication kb:entity-sets now warns about, and would diverge from the question path the first time either is tuned. Factor a shared scorer; keep the 7 existing tests passing as the regression gate." ;
    pred:remaining "Not built. Factor routeQuestion's scorer to accept N statements; a deselect affordance on Add; a ranked destination picker showing WHY each graph ranked (which subjects/predicates matched); the no-match outcome above." .

