kb:import-target-resolution
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/storage/__tests__/kb-import-target.test.ts" ;
    pred:has-status "functional" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:evidence "MEASURED 2026-08-13 in Matt's own registry: FIVE duplicated names (reckons-production, reckons-roadmap, starter-everyday, starter-quickstart, starter-visual-review), each covering more than one independent copy, several never opened. Three of the four import paths already resolved a target correctly — drive-sync matches stableId then name, workspace import skips known names and stableIds, the docs-leap path reuses a found entry — while the FILE IMPORT at src/routes/(app)/ingest/+page.svelte called createKb() with no registry check of any kind. The duplicated names are exactly static/*.ttl filenames minus their extension, which is what that page derives a name from." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:multi-kb ;
    pred:description "One shared rule deciding where an imported graph lands: replace an existing graph, ask the user, or create a new one. Removes the cause of duplicated graph names rather than only reporting them." ;
    pred:actual-deps "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:principle "IDENTITY IS WHAT MAKES DUPLICATE FILES HARMLESS. Several copies of one graph resolve to one entry and update it in place; several ANONYMOUS copies can only ever become several graphs. The fix is therefore not to forbid copies — a local-first tool cannot — but to make every copy say what it is." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:graph-sets ;
    pred:feature-id "F127" ;
    pred:constraint "REPLACING MUST ACTUALLY REPLACE. The ingest path wrote into an existing database without clearing it first, so a replace would have left old facts beside new ones and silently doubled the graph. statements and sources are now cleared inside the replace branch." ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:constraint "THE FIX INTRODUCES ITS OWN HAZARD, AND IT IS GUARDED. Once every copy carries an identity, an identity match makes replacement automatic — so importing a STALE export from an abandoned workspace root would silently roll a newer graph back. That copy is correctly identified and still the wrong thing to restore. resolveImportTarget now parses the exporter's `# generated <ISO>` header and downgrades a stale identity match from 'replace' to 'ambiguous' with its own wording, while an UNKNOWN timestamp still replaces so hand-written TTL stays importable. 18 tests." ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/storage> ;
    pred:remaining "BUILT: src/lib/storage/kb-import-target.ts (resolveImportTarget, uniqueKbName), 11 tests, wired into the ingest file-import path, which now also reports 'Updated' rather than 'Created' when it replaced. NOT BUILT: the five EXISTING duplicate pairs are untouched — the graphs page still only reports them, and which copy is real remains a judgement about content that no heuristic should make. A merge-or-discard affordance on that notice is the follow-up." ;
    pred:decided "THE TWO SIGNALS ARE NOT EQUALLY STRONG, and conflating them is how an import destroys work. A STABLE ID match means 'this IS that graph, newer' — replacing in place is correct, and ingestExistingKb takes a recovery snapshot first. A NAME match means 'possibly the same graph': 'roadmap.ttl' from two different projects collides trivially, so a name match warns and offers the choice, and the SAFE branch (keep both, suffixed readably) is the default. Overwriting on a name match would be a data-loss bug dressed as deduplication." ;
    rdfs:label "Re-importing a graph updates it instead of duplicating it" ;
    pred:decided "IDENTITY IS MINTED AT EXPORT, WHICH IS THE HALF THAT ACTUALLY PREVENTS DUPLICATION (Matt, 2026-08-13: 'the export procedure should work different to avoid getting multiple copies of the same kb out of sync'). syncAllKbs read `settings?.kbStableId` and passed it straight through, so a graph that had never been given a stable id exported a file with NO IDENTITY IN IT — and on re-import there was nothing to match on but the name. Verified against the real files: none of static/kbs/*/*.ttl, kbs/*/*.ttl or the canonical static/*.ttl carried a kbStableId. The export now mints one via getOrCreateStableId (which already existed and was unused here) and persists it to the graph's settings AND the registry BEFORE writing any file, so the id in the file always matches the id in the app." ;
    pred:actual-files "4"^^xsd:integer .

kb:multi-graph-viewport
    rdfs:label "Open a graph SET — several graphs in one viewport, separated by distance" ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/rdf/kb-leap.ts" ;
    pred:estimated-files "12"^^xsd:integer ;
