kb:fact-trust-tiers
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:part-of kb:context-engine ;
    pred:description "Matt, 2026-08-15: 'Automated findings that are verified are useful, and fact judged by humans even more useful.' Today ReviewStatus has pending / pending-removal / confirmed / refined / rejected / superseded, and every automated finding lands in the same 'pending' bucket as a model's guess. A deterministic check that PROVED something deserves to outrank a plausible suggestion without pretending to outrank a person." ;
    pred:feature-id "F135.1" ;
    pred:decided "'VERIFIED' MUST MEAN RE-CHECKABLE, NOT MERELY MACHINE-PRODUCED. A script emitting a finding is not evidence; a script that can be RE-RUN to prove the finding is. So a verified statement carries the NAME of the check that establishes it, and that check must be runnable on demand — 'integrations-tech.ttl does not parse' is verifiable (re-parse it), while 'this file looks fragile' is a judgement wearing a script's clothes and stays a suggestion. Without that rule 'verified' degrades into 'a computer said it', which is the exact authority-laundering kb:honest-status exists to prevent." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:content-safety ;
    pred:open-question "Does a verified automated fact enter the graph WITHOUT human review, or does it enter as a distinct status a human can still overrule? Entering unreviewed is what makes the tier worth having and is also the point where an automated writer starts editing the user's graph — kb:tenet-private and the F52 control model both bear on this, and it is Matt's call." ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:estimated-deps "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/rdf/types.ts" ;
    pred:evidence "THE COST OF NOT HAVING THIS IS ON RECORD. The review queue reached 904 entries with verified defects and speculative suggestions indistinguishable in the same bucket, and a TRUE finding — 'integrations-tech.ttl does not parse' — was re-reported fifty-nine times and never acted on, because nothing marked it as proven rather than proposed. It was two bad lines in a 944-line graph and took minutes to fix once seen." ;
    pred:estimated-files "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:label "Trust tiers — verified automation ranks below human judgement, above a guess" .

