    pred:has-file "scripts/offline/lib/graph-grounding.ts" ;
    pred:description "Every recurring task is routed to the cheapest tier that can do it correctly, decided by the first test it passes: (1) SCRIPT — the answer is checkable by a rule (does this path exist, does this parse, is this status in the enum), so it is deterministic code, zero tokens, zero hallucination, runs in CI and fails loudly; (2) LOCAL AGENT — the answer is judgment over language and being wrong is cheap because the output is a PROPOSAL a human gates (first-pass code review, description drafting, staleness reads), always emitted to knowledge.pending.jsonl, never to source; (3) OPUS — cross-file architectural reasoning, deciding the process, triaging the queue the other tiers fill, and writing code that lands. Opus designs the harness; the local model is a plugin inside it (ground -> prompt -> validate -> emit-proposal, per the PR #43 devstral salvage). Promotion ladder: anything Opus does twice becomes an agent job or a script; anything an agent gets right RELIABLY is demoted to a script, because reliability proves the rule was expressible." ;
