kb:code-graph-edges
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:description "Matt, 2026-08-14: 'shouldn't the code graph have detailed connections for concepts, across multiple files?' It should. static/reckons-codebase.ttl had has-file and tested-by and nothing joining one module to another except skos:broader, which is containment rather than dependency. scripts/offline/derive-code-edges.ts derives kpred:depends-on-module from static TypeScript imports." ;
    pred:test-coverage "none" ;
    rdfs:label "Concept-to-concept edges in the code graph, derived from imports" ;
    pred:measured "395 source files, 944 resolvable internal imports, 80 module-to-module edges; 38 written after dropping 42 that carried fewer than three imports as noise rather than structure. Heaviest couplings: routes->stores (71), components->stores (53), routes->rdf (41)." ;
    pred:honest-note "FILE GRANULARITY, NOT SYMBOL — and the gap matters. '154 files import types.ts' is true and coarse: changing one exported type does not touch all 154, and this cannot tell which did. Static imports only, so the dynamic `await import()` this codebase uses heavily in stores is invisible, and type-only imports count the same as value imports, so coupling is over-stated. The number is an upper bound on impact, useful for warning and wrong for planning precisely." ;
    pred:principle "A DEPENDENCY EDGE REPLACES A CONVENTION WITH A MEASUREMENT. scope-derive.ts offers a starting estimate as 30% of a module's file count — a stated convention with nothing behind it. A blast radius is computed: change a file and the graph knows which files import it. That is the difference between a number someone chose and a number the code entails." ;
    pred:feature-id "F130.4" ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
    pred:honest-note "UNTESTED, DECLARED (2026-08-14, caught by status-evidence). The import resolver and module aggregation live INSIDE scripts/offline/derive-code-edges.ts and generate-file-graph.ts rather than in an importable module, so there is nothing a unit test can reach without extracting them first. Its output is checkable by running it — 509 file entities and 981 edges that parse — but that is verification by inspection, not a regression guard, and this logic now feeds scope estimates, so a silent break would corrupt every derived number." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:serena-prior-art ;
    pred:evidence "IT IMMEDIATELY MEASURED SOMETHING THAT SHOULD HAVE CHANGED MY BEHAVIOUR EARLIER TODAY: src/lib/rdf/types.ts is imported DIRECTLY BY 154 FILES, 226 transitively, spanning 17 modules — far and away the highest blast radius in the repo. I edited it twice this session (Statement.proposedBy for F129, then Statement.findingClass for F130) without knowing that. Nothing warned, because until now the graph could not say it." ;
    pred:part-of kb:scope-estimate-derivation ;
    pred:remaining "Feed the blast radius into scope-derive so suggestEstimate stops using a fraction; surface a warning when a change touches a high-blast-radius file; and resolve dynamic imports, which currently make the graph silently under-count coupling in exactly the module (stores) that has the most of them." ;
    pred:has-status "functional" .

