kb:graph-economics
    pred:constraint "words * 1.33 — the project's own estimateTokens (mcp-server/src/index.ts, mirrored at scripts/offline/prompt-audit.ts:27). Every figure must use it so results stay comparable with the compression bench." ;
    pred:principle "A saving claimed without its cost is not a measurement, it is marketing. The graph's DEBIT — TTL authoring and maintenance churn, MCP tool-schema tax paid on every request, and the triage cost of agent-tier proposals — must be counted in the same ledger as its credit, or the threshold cannot be stated at all." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:agent-context-dogfooding ;
    pred:remaining "Not built. scripts/offline/graph-economics.ts, its jobs.json entry (tier=script, non-blocking — a ledger is advisory), and the seeded JSONL ledger." ;
    pred:description "SCRIPT tier (F74.3): deterministic, zero tokens, zero triage. scripts/offline/graph-economics.ts assembles both sides of the ledger and prints the break-even. DEBIT: TTL churn from git log --numstat over static/*.ttl (commits, lines, tokens written); the MCP tool-schema tax summed from the kb_* tool definitions, reported in BOTH modes (eager — paid every request — and deferred/ToolSearch, which give very different break-evens); and the agent-tier triage cost, which is DECLARED UNMEASURED rather than silently omitted. CREDIT: compressed-subgraph vs whole-corpus tokens recomputed from the live corpus (not quoted), plus an avoided-rework ledger. OUTPUTS: break-even in queries-before-payback per mode, and a compounding curve walking git history monthly (corpus triples vs cumulative maintenance churn vs cumulative modelled saving) — the first actual evidence for or against the compounding claim." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:context-compression ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:session-tokens ;
    rdfs:label "Graph economics ledger (break-even + compounding)" ;
    pred:part-of kb:work-tiering ;
    pred:open-question "Avoided rework — the likely LARGEST benefit (a duplicate feature not built costs nothing forever) — cannot be derived from git. Backed instead by an append-only ledger at reckons-workspace/graph-economics.jsonl, one entry per avoided duplicate, each CITING the entity that prevented it. Semi-manual and honest; a fabricated automatic count would be worse than none." ;
    pred:honest-note "CAUSATION IS NOT AVAILABLE HERE, and the report must not imply it. Cohesion improves for many reasons — refactors, review, taste, a quiet week — and there is NO COUNTERFACTUAL: no control repo built without a graph, and n=1. So the harness reports (a) the trend, and (b) per-event attribution where a commit or session actually CITES the entity that redirected it, and never a bare causal claim that the graph produced the trend. An honest correlation plus a handful of attributed events is worth more than a confident number that cannot survive the question 'compared to what?'." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:cost-awareness ;
    pred:dimension "COHESION (Matt, 2026-07-19) — for a software project the gain is not only rework avoided but code that stays INTEGRATED: the graph steers a session into extending an existing module rather than adding a parallel one. Four deterministic signals, three of which are already built. (1) EXTEND-VS-ADD RATIO — per feature commit, lines added to EXISTING files vs lines in NEWLY CREATED files, from git --numstat. This is the direct measure of 'enhanced the current feature instead of writing a new one' and is the one signal not yet computed anywhere. (2) DUPLICATED BLOCK-GROUPS over time, from scripts/offline/code-sprawl.ts. (3) PLAN-LEVEL OVERLAP WARNINGS — features sharing a hub but no file — from scripts/offline/shared-deps.ts. (4) THE GRAPH'S OWN COHESION — singleton predicate-type share from graph-lint, since a graph whose predicates generalize is itself more navigable." ;
    pred:constraint "REUSE THE EXISTING DETECTORS. code-sprawl.ts and shared-deps.ts already compute (2) and (3) deterministically; graph-economics.ts must INVOKE them (adding --json output to each) rather than reimplement their logic. Reimplementing a duplication detector inside the economics script would be precisely the sprawl code-sprawl.ts exists to catch — and the harness would fail its own metric." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:feature-id "F74.5" ;
    pred:honest-note "Report the result whichever way it falls. If the threshold is not yet crossed on tokens alone, say so plainly and let the avoided-rework ledger carry the argument — a ledger that always shows a profit is not a record." ;
    pred:measured "2026-07-19: a request for a 'new' node-summarization feature was resolved by ~2k tokens of kb_search onto existing F65 / F96 / kb:graph-legibility, instead of building a parallel feature under a different name. First entry in the avoided-rework ledger." .

kb:timeline-undated-lane
    pred:decided "MATT, 2026-08-13: the undated lane, over hiding undated nodes entirely (93% of the starter graph would vanish on switching layout) and over keeping them placed while fixing only the range (the wall remains, still claiming a date it does not have). Placing an undated node at its ingestion time is the graph asserting a date it does not have, in the one view whose entire job is to say when things happened." ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
    pred:description "Settles the F59 open question Matt left UNDECIDED, and fixes the 'starter-graph timeline force still looks bad' item carried in HANDOFF since 2026-07-31. In event mode a node with no recognised temporal predicate now goes to a labelled UNDATED LANE below the axis instead of being placed at its statement's createdAt." ;
    pred:remaining "BUILT: src/lib/rdf/timeline-layout.ts (buildNodeTimes, timelineRange, undatedCount), 14 tests, both renderers wired to it, lane spread over 5 rows clear of the dated band and labelled 'no date (N)'. NOT DONE: the camera does not auto-fit the axis plus lane, so the layout needs a manual zoom-out to see whole; and 165 parked nodes remain inherently dense — clustering or collapsing the lane is a further step." ;
    pred:actual-deps "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:part-of kb:spatial-force-layout ;
    pred:actual-files "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/timeline-layout.test.ts" ;
    pred:evidence "THE BUG WAS BIGGER THAN A COSMETIC ONE, and it is measured. Both renderers fell back to createdAt — the INGESTION time — for undated nodes and placed them as if that were an event. On starter-everyday.ttl only 12 of 177 nodes carry a date, so 93% were placed by import time; starter-guide.ttl has 216 nodes and NOT ONE date, so 100% were. Worse than the resulting wall of nodes: those fake timestamps entered dataMin/dataMax, so the axis spanned 36 days and the real 4-day trip was compressed into 11.1% of it. Measured in the running app against the real graph." ;
    pred:evidence "THE LANE WAS ALREADY WRITTEN AND UNREACHABLE. Both renderers contained an else-branch placing undated nodes at y = -SPREAD_Y * 0.7 — dead code, because the createdAt fallback guaranteed every node received a time and the branch never ran. The fix largely made the existing intent actually happen." ;
    pred:feature-id "F59.2" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:known-issue "THREE FURTHER DEFECTS FOUND IN THE SAME CODE AND FIXED. (1) In 3D, `if (useIngested) A else if (!useIngested) A` — byte-identical branches reading as though they distinguished cases. (2) In 2D, getTimelineDataRange (which bounds the right-click scrub) EXCLUDED the createdAt fallback while buildTimelineAnchors2D INCLUDED it, so the scrub bounds and the node positions disagreed and dragging felt broken. (3) The recognised temporal predicates existed in THREE copies — KnowledgeGraph, KnowledgeGraph2D and parse-date.ts — which is the drift parse-date.ts's own comment exists to prevent; all now read the one set." ;
    rdfs:label "Undated nodes get a lane, not a fake date" ;
    pred:has-status "functional" .

kb:risk-evidence-contract
    pred:progress "DEPENDENCY + SECURITY REVIEW 2026-08-16 (NO PACKAGE CHANGE). npm audit --omit=dev reports 0 production vulnerabilities (155 production packages). The full lockfile has six dev/build paths, 4 high and 2 moderate, with no critical: direct @sveltejs/kit 2.70.0 plus brace-expansion 2.1.3/5.0.8, fast-uri 3.1.4, nanoid 3.3.15, postcss 8.5.19 and undici 7.28.0. Audit fix --dry-run proposes compatible updates only: Kit 2.70.2, brace-expansion 2.1.4/5.0.9, fast-uri 3.1.5, nanoid 3.3.18, postcss 8.5.26 and undici 7.29.0. The current override test passes but its brace-expansion floors still accept the vulnerable versions, so tighten it before treating it as a supply-chain regression gate. Overrides are intentional and observed resolved: uuid root-pin aligns Hume/Storybook, cookie constrains Kit, sharp aligns Transformers, and exact adm-zip constrains ONNX Runtime; retain their compatibility test." ;
    pred:decided "REPORT CONTRACT. EvidenceReport carries plan id, git base/head/diff hash, environment/tool versions, command argv, start/end time, exit code, parsed counts, artifact hashes and an explicit unverified list. The runner captures process results directly; an agent may select or explain checks but cannot write PASS. A retry appends a new run rather than replacing the failed evidence." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:release-pipeline ;
    pred:progress "TOOLING/CONTROL WARNINGS 2026-08-16. Storybook core/svelte adapters resolve at 10.5.2 while addon-essentials and @storybook/test are 8.6.18 with Storybook-8 peers; npm ls marks the installed tree peer-invalid. This is a release-tooling reliability gap, not a static-app production vulnerability: align the entire family to one supported major before using story builds as gate evidence. package.json says 0.2.0 while package-lock root metadata says 0.1.0; npm ci --dry-run succeeds, but synchronize on the next deliberate dependency update. secret-scan finds no inline provider secret; CSP origin audit passes; safety attestation passes 6/6 with its normal npm PATH. Its direct use of ambient npx causes false indeterminate Vitest/graph-lint results in a Node-only shell; resolve local binaries directly so the verifier's environment cannot be misreported as a failed safety control. Deprecated boolean/rdf-dataset-ext/source-map leaves are parent-owned maintenance signals, not a reason for untested direct overrides." ;
    pred:description "Give every material change a pre-work VerificationPlan and a machine-produced post-work EvidenceReport. The plan states what behavior and risk are in scope; the report records what fresh checks actually ran. This formalizes the project's existing test, mutation, graph-lint and safety discipline without importing another agent skill or trusting prose in a handoff." ;
    pred:decided "RISK MATRIX. Low-risk prose/metadata runs syntax and graph/diff checks. Normal logic runs targeted tests, types and the full unit suite. Data/serialization/sync/security/egress/concurrency work additionally requires round-trip or recovery tests, property/mutation/hostile-input checks where applicable, secret/supply-chain checks and real execution. Visual/interaction work adds device, orientation, touch and observable-outcome evidence. The matrix is a minimum, never proof the spec is complete." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:remaining "DONE WHEN a command such as `npm run verify -- --feature F136` resolves the feature's plan, runs the risk-required checks, writes one append-only report and generates the handoff verification block; injected command failure is recorded as failure; an omitted required gate stays unverified; and changing the diff invalidates reuse of an older report." ;
    pred:touches-file "scripts/offline/run-all.ts" ;
    pred:feature-id "F34.1" ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:decided "PLAN CONTRACT. VerificationPlan carries feature/task id, base revision, intended behavior with positive and negative examples, explicit non-goals, touched modules/data boundaries, risk tags, required checks and qualitative approvals. The plan is reviewable before implementation. Automatic inference may raise risk; lowering an inferred gate requires a recorded rationale and, for data-loss/security/egress risk, explicit human approval." ;
    pred:priority "medium" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:claim-settlement ;
    pred:depends-on kb:work-tiering ;
    pred:constraint "CALCULABLE EVIDENCE CANNOT SETTLE QUALITATIVE STATUS. A green suite can establish that named checks passed; it cannot declare the UX good, the architecture complete or a feature production-ready. Those remain separately attributed human judgements under F135.2. Unrun means unverified, never pass." ;
    rdfs:label "Risk-scaled verification plans and fresh evidence reports" ;
    pred:constraint "THE VERIFIER IS ALSO A CLAIMANT. Evidence includes versions and rerunnable commands, and high-risk mappings need mutation/fresh-context checks so a broken checker cannot authenticate itself merely by exiting zero. Git hashes order the record but do not make its timing impossible to rewrite." ;
    pred:part-of kb:deep-testing ;
    pred:progress "REMEDIATED 2026-08-16. Removed obsolete Storybook-8 addon-essentials and @storybook/test root dependencies; the already-empty Storybook-10 addons configuration relies on the built-ins as intended, and its stale Storybook-8 heading was corrected. Storybook build now passes and npm ls has no peer-invalid Storybook tree. Raised the direct Kit floor to ^2.70.2; the audit lock update resolves brace-expansion 2.1.4/5.0.9, fast-uri 3.1.5, nanoid 3.3.18, postcss 8.5.26 and undici 7.29.0. The lock-root metadata now matches package version 0.2.0. Fresh full and production-only audits both report 0 vulnerabilities. Override behavior is unchanged, but its test now rejects the previous vulnerable brace-expansion floors and passes. Safety attestation executes checked-in vitest/tsx through process.execPath rather than ambient npx, so its direct Node-only invocation passes 6/6 instead of falsely reporting unrun controls. Full unit suite (146 files/2,016 tests), type check (0 errors/81 existing warnings), production, Storybook and extension builds all pass. FOLLOW-UP: Rolldown documents inlineDynamicImports false as the default and codeSplitting false as the opposite single-bundle behavior. The redundant deprecated false flag was removed, and Vite 8 build.rollupOptions was renamed build.rolldownOptions; a new extension build preserved the six expected entries, passed and emitted no deprecation warning." ;
    pred:touches-file "scripts/offline/status-evidence.ts" .

