kb:int-grist
    pred:relates-to kb:structured-data ;
    pred:principle "MAP TO GRIST'S GRAIN, NOT TO A GENERIC GRID. A table becomes a named graph, a row becomes an entity keyed by its stable row id, a column becomes a predicate, and — the part that matters — a FORMULA column becomes a derived predicate whose provenance is the formula text plus the document revision that produced the value. That is what makes an imported total defensible instead of a number of unknown parentage, and it is the same discipline F113 applies to observations: the method travels with the finding." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:integration-plugin-sdk ;
    pred:provides "self-hosted structured tables with formula columns" ;
    pred:honest-note "SPECULATIVE, NOTHING BUILT (2026-07-31). No Grist code, no connector, no settings field. The capability claims above are recorded from general knowledge as of this model's May 2026 training cutoff and have NOT been verified against a running Grist instance or its current API documentation — treat the endpoint shapes, the formula-column behavior and the licensing as things to confirm first, not as findings. A spike against a local Docker instance is the honest first step." ;
    pred:open-question "Change detection and auth. Does the app poll the document for revisions or receive a webhook, and does the connector authenticate with a user API key held in settings like the other integrations, or is something OAuth-shaped needed for a hosted instance? Both need checking against a running server before any estimate is trusted." ;
