    pred:evidence "clickswave/silocat (AGPL-3.0, 10 stars) is a working reference for encrypted sharing: XChaCha20-Poly1305 with Argon2id-derived keys applied client-side BEFORE upload, so the server holds ciphertext it cannot open — and it states its own limit out loud, that zero-knowledge is not zero-metadata, since sizes and timestamps stay visible. This roadmap mentions encryption once. A shared graph package is plaintext today, and F122 has just decided that retained third-party source copies must never travel in one. AGPL means read it, do not vendor it — scripts/offline/competitor-scan.ts already flags copyleft for exactly this reason." ;
