kb:predicate-threshold-limit
    pred:relates-to kb:vocabulary-grounding ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Concept> ;
    rdfs:label "Cosine alone cannot separate a synonym from an opposite" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:entity-normalization ;
    pred:honest-note "THE RANKING IN THE EXISTING EMBEDDING BENCH DOES NOT TRANSFER TO THIS DECISION. Models are compared there on entity similarity in coarse bands (0.7/0.4); a model chosen on that basis could false-merge three quarters of the distinct predicate pairs here. Run npm run bench:predicates BEFORE changing the embedding model, and read the false-merge column first." ;
    pred:measurement "MEASURED 2026-08-15 via npm run bench:predicates. bge-small-en-v1.5 (the shipped default): 16.7% merge recall, 0% false merges, separation -0.256 — SAFE but nearly inert, and it MISSES the real observed case (has-heart-count/has-number-of-hearts at 0.803, below the 0.88 line). all-MiniLM-L6-v2: 8.3% / 0% / -0.311. nomic-embed-text: 16.7% / 0% / -0.208. gte-small: 66.7% recall but 58.3% FALSE merges. e5-small-v2: 83.3% recall and 75% FALSE merges, scoring has-predator/has-prey at 0.9322 and has-min-weight/has-max-weight at 0.9330." ;
    pred:description "normalize-entities.ts rewrites an incoming predicate onto an existing one at cosine >= 0.88. Benchmarked against five embedding models on 12 synonym pairs and 12 lexically-similar-but-distinct pairs, EVERY model showed NEGATIVE separation: its worst true synonym scored below its closest distinct pair. No single threshold separates the two classes, so tuning the constant only trades one error for the other." ;
    pred:decided "KEEP 0.88 AND DO NOT CHASE RECALL BY LOWERING IT. The distinct pair is-found-in/is-located-in scores 0.8341 with the shipped model — ABOVE the 0.8030 synonym we would be lowering the line to catch. Any threshold low enough to fix the observed vocabulary drift merges a distinction the graph author drew first. The recall belongs at extraction time (F136), not in a similarity threshold." ;
    pred:constraint "THE TWO ERRORS COST DIFFERENT AMOUNTS AND MUST NEVER BE AVERAGED. A missed merge leaves a duplicate predicate the review queue still shows a human. A FALSE merge rewrites a fact into a different fact before anyone sees it. Any composite score over the two lets a model buy recall with silent corruption — which is exactly how e5-small-v2 would look like an upgrade." ;
    pred:tested-by "tests/bench/predicate-vocab-scoring.test.ts" .

