kb:loop-job-grouping
    pred:grouping-axis "TOPICAL RELEVANCE (Matt, 2026-07-19) — a SECOND, independent axis. One ingested article carries several subjects, and the ones incidental to the article's own core points are noise against the graph's goal. Cluster a single source's extracted triples by subject cluster so an off-topic cluster can be rejected wholesale, rather than declined one triple at a time. Reuses the embedding path already in the app (src/lib/embed.ts, BGE-small-en-v1.5) — the same similarity machinery kb:entity-normalization uses — so no new model is introduced." ;
    pred:part-of kb:autonomous-loop ;
    pred:description "Review cost scales with the number of DECISIONS, not the number of facts. Forty facts from one agent about one entity, all of the same kind, are ONE decision presented forty times. Group the queue by (task, agent, subject, gate) and let a group be accepted, rejected, or opened in a single act — with the outliers in a group surfaced rather than hidden, because a batch accept is exactly where a bad fact slips through." ;
    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:constraint "A JOB GROUP IS A SET (Matt, 2026-07-19). This phase does not get its own grouping mechanism: it instantiates ktype:EntitySet + has-member over PENDING STATEMENTS, the same primitive kb:entity-sets uses over entities and kb:agent-orchestration will use over tasks. See kb:entity-sets for the one-primitive-three-consumers principle. Consequence: a review group is queryable, round-trips in TTL, and can be spotlighted on the canvas for free — because it is the same node type the graph already renders." ;
    rdfs:label "Phase 4 — group the queue so it can be judged in one pass" ;
    pred:principle "Batching must make the ODD ONE OUT more visible, not less. A group that hides its dissenter has converted review into rubber-stamping." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Phase> ;
    pred:grouping-axis "PROVENANCE — (task, agent, subject, gate). Groups facts by where they came from and what produced them." ;
    pred:constraint "Outlier highlighting is a PRECONDITION of accept-all, not a follow-up. kb:review-attention holds the opposing principle ('granularity breeds rubber-stamping... trains the human to accept all'), and this entity's own principle says a group that hides its dissenter has converted review into rubber-stamping. So a group surfaces its off-centroid / low-confidence members BEFORE the accept-all control is offered, and accept-all applies only to the currently FILTERED group, stating the count it is about to confirm." ;
    pred:remaining "Grouping in the review queue; batch accept/reject; outlier highlighting within a group; the topical-relevance axis above. Implemented over src/lib/rdf/entity-sets.ts, NOT as a parallel grouping mechanism." .

