    pred:proof "Functional 2026-07-30: F97 HAS AN ENTRY POINT. src/lib/rdf/archive-sweep.ts plans an age sweep purely (19 unit tests, mutation-checked five ways) and sweepArchiveByAge performs it via the existing runArchive ordering guarantee (43 adapter tests). /kb carries an 'archive old events' control on the current graph: set a day threshold, read a plan naming what WILL and WILL NOT move, confirm, and the facts move to the '<parent> (archives)' graph and appear in the gallery. Proven in a real browser end to end — tests/e2e/archive-sweep.test.ts (7 tests) asserts the facts LEFT the working Dexie database, not merely the view. Full suite 1,441 tests, 0 type errors." ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/storage> ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/archive-sweep.test.ts" ;
    pred:principle "Retention is part of the foundation because the storage cost is structural, not incidental. Shipping snapshots without a bound would trade a node-count problem for a bigger storage problem and call it an improvement." ;
    pred:has-file "src/lib/storage/archive-store.ts" ;
    pred:honest-note "THE GALLERY DISPLAY IS BUILT AND BROWSER-VERIFIED, THE SWEEP THAT FILLS IT IS NOT (2026-07-29). An archive graph now renders nested under the graph whose history it holds on /kb, badged, with its fact count — src/lib/storage/archive-gallery.ts (pure grouping, 13 unit tests, mutation-checked) plus tests/e2e/archive-gallery.test.ts (6 tests, real browser). It handles the imperfect links deliberately: a legacy archive linked by parent NAME rather than stableId is still adopted, and an archive whose parent has left the registry stays listed and says so, because retained-but-unreachable history is only technically preserved. BUT THE STATUS STAYS 'scaffolded' BECAUSE NOTHING IN THE APP CREATES AN ARCHIVE: grepping src/ for runArchive and ensureArchiveKb finds no caller outside archive-store.ts and its tests. There is no 'archive now' action, no age-threshold setting, and no sweep — so a user cannot yet produce an archive to see in this display, and F97's own headline ('auto-archive of events older than a configurable threshold') is unbuilt. The display is correct and proven against seeded data; that is a smaller claim than 'the feature works' and is deliberately not written as one." ;
    pred:feature-id "F97.1" ;
    pred:has-file "src/lib/rdf/archive-sweep.ts" ;
    pred:description "Foundation phase. Creates the '<name> (archives)' graph on demand via the existing kb-registry, links it to its parent by stableId, and writes an event journal: one reified event per destructive operation (delete, merge, prune, age-drop) carrying timestamp, actor, affected entities, and a FULL pre-operation graph snapshot. Retention ships in this phase, not after it — full snapshots make unbounded growth a certainty, so the writer enforces a policy (keep last N + milestone snapshots) from the first commit." ;
    pred:has-file "src/lib/rdf/archive.ts" ;
    pred:honest-note "SCAFFOLDED, not functional: the foundation now stores and bounds real snapshots, but no production delete, merge, prune or age-drop path imports runArchive yet. F97 itself remains planned; an unwired archive engine does not trim a user's graph." ;
    pred:proof "Scaffolded 2026-07-28: the adapter writes complete pre-operation Statement objects as event-linked RDF JSON payloads, reloads them without repurposing statement id or provenance, survives the annotated Turtle export/import path, and enforces the bounded default (latest 10 snapshots plus milestones) before touching the working graph. Retention removes payload rows only; every journal event remains. Archive lookup now uses the parent's stableId rather than its display name, follows parent renames without creating another archive, separates same-named parents, upgrades legacy name links, and requires an exact registered working Dexie database id carrying that same stableId before a destructive write. Focused pure + adapter suite: 74 tests; full suite: 1,359 tests." ;
    pred:tested-by "tests/visual/user-stories/archive-sweep.test.ts" ;
    pred:honest-note "THE SWEEP IS MANUAL, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE GAP BETWEEN THIS PHASE AND F97 (2026-07-30). Nothing sweeps on its own: there is no schedule, no age-threshold trigger and no proactive nudge, so F97's headline word 'AUTO' remains unbuilt and kb:auto-archive stays in-progress rather than functional. The control is offered on the CURRENT graph only, because a sweep works from the loaded in-memory store and reaching into an unloaded graph's database to move facts the user is not looking at is a different and more dangerous operation. Three deliberate conservatisms, each reported to the user rather than hidden: an UNDATED entity is never swept (falling back to ingest time would silently become 'archive what I imported a while ago'); an entity is judged by its NEWEST date, so a long-running thing touched last week is current; and an entity carrying UNREVIEWED facts is held back, because archiving by subject-or-object would carry pending facts out of the review queue where nothing would ever surface them again." ;
    pred:honest-note "A REAL BUG WAS FOUND ONLY BY LOOKING AT A FAILURE SCREENSHOT (2026-07-30): the first live sweep threw DataCloneError, because Dexie stores structured clones and a Svelte 5 $state array hands out Proxies that structuredClone refuses. Every unit suite was green throughout — a mocked Dexie clones nothing — and the gap had never fired because until this phase NOTHING in src/ called runArchive with live store state. Fixed inside runArchive (not at the call site, since a forgetful caller would throw between the archive write and the working-graph delete) and pinned by a test that runs structuredClone over what was written. A second look at the phone screenshot showed the one destructive control rendering as borderless coral text that read as a hyperlink, inherited from button.danger; the affordance is restored and asserted. This is the same lesson as the gallery's --warn bug: determinism buys 'the rule fired', never 'the rule was right'." ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/storage/__tests__/archive-store.test.ts" ;
    rdfs:label "Archive graph + snapshot journal + retention" ;
    pred:depends-on kb:auto-archive ;
    pred:has-status "functional" .

