    pred:proof "The MOAT — the grounding CONSTRAINT — is built and tested (9 tests, 2026-07-15), which is the half that matters (the description says so: 'the moat is the grounding constraint, not the generation'). generation-grounding.ts validateGeneration() enforces the render-step contract: every generated sentence must cite >=1 statement, every citation must exist, and at least one must be CONFIRMED — uncited (hallucination), dangling, and unconfirmed citations are each caught. It is the generation-side analog of kb:passage-grounding (grounding.ts, ingest side). Pure/deterministic: it verifies the citation contract, not the paraphrase (that stays a model's job). SCAFFOLDED not functional: the actual grounded GENERATOR (emit prose WITH per-sentence citations) is not built, and nothing wires this validator into the doc/page/tooltip render paths yet — so today it enforces a contract no producer emits." ;
