    pred:part-of kb:co-orchestration ;
    pred:description "Shelly's action vocabulary grows along ONE axis: things that require the user. ASK — when Shelly does not know, it emits a partial fact (object '?', plus what it blocks) rather than guessing; a guess silently entered into a knowledge graph is worse than a stalled task. ANSWER — Shelly walks the user through the pending queue conversationally, so the review backlog can be cleared by talking instead of clicking. ATTEST — a fact the user supplies is written with verifiable-by `user`, never laundered into looking verified. It does NOT gain: a shell, a file editor, or a code writer." ;
