kb:antonym-pairs-dead-entries
    pred:relates-to kb:antonym-write-guard ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Concept> ;
    pred:description "FOUND 2026-08-15 while building the predicate benchmark. semantic-diff.ts stored antonym pairs in hyphenated form (is-true/is-false) while every caller passed a label from labelFromIRI, which has ALREADY converted hyphens to spaces. So the substring test 'is true'.includes('is-true') was false and NINE of the pairs — including is-true/is-false, the most consequential contradiction a knowledge graph can hold — could never match anything. Fixed by splitting both sides on either separator and comparing whole words." ;
    pred:principle "A LOOKUP TABLE IS NOT A CONTROL UNTIL SOMETHING PROVES IT FIRES. These nine entries read correctly, reviewed correctly, and did nothing for as long as they existed, because no test ever asserted a match — only that the surrounding logic behaved given an assumed one. The same shape as a mock-vector test standing in for a real threshold measurement." ;
    rdfs:label "Nine antonym pairs that never once fired" .

