kb:scope-justification
    pred:description "Matt, 2026-08-14: 'The idea here is to raise judgement to the human and council. The goal being judgement is made by higher reasoning models and a human that can be accountable for the decision. justifications may be added ... the engineer or the designer may have justification for the increase.' Creep opens a decision; this carries why, who decided, and what they decided." ;
    rdfs:label "Justifying a scope increase — judgement raised to a human or the council" ;
    pred:remaining "A surface that asks for the justification when creep is detected; persistence of justifications as graph facts; and the council lane actually invoking F102 rather than naming it." ;
    pred:decided "STRUCTURED KIND AND PROSE, NOT ONE OR THE OTHER. Both examples Matt gave are recurring KINDS rather than one-offs — 'I used the initial version and it now clearly needs this other thing' is discovery-through-use; 'if we change this here we would change these other places for consistency and maintainability' is consistency-maintenance. Naming the kinds makes repeated causes COUNTABLE, which free text cannot be: a design whose creep is repeatedly discovery-through-use was under-specified in a different way from one whose creep is repeatedly consistency-maintenance, and only the first is fixed by thinking harder up front. The engineer's own words are kept alongside." ;
    pred:feature-id "F130.3" ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/scope-derive.test.ts" ;
    pred:part-of kb:scope-creep ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:decided "ACCOUNTABILITY IS A NAMED PARTY, NEVER 'the system'. isAccountable() returns false for a decision with no decider, however it is labelled, and an undecided increase stays OPEN rather than defaulting to approved — silence is not consent, and the F52 boundary applies to scope exactly as it applies to facts." ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
    pred:relates-to kb:poseidons-council ;
    pred:honest-note "SCAFFOLDED, NOT FUNCTIONAL: the model and its routing are built and tested (20 tests), and NOTHING PRODUCES A JUSTIFICATION YET. No UI collects one, scope-check does not prompt for one, and no justification has ever been recorded — so the council and human lanes are defined and unexercised." ;
    pred:has-status "scaffolded" ;
    pred:principle "AN ACCEPTED JUSTIFICATION THAT CHANGES NOTHING IS A RUBBER STAMP. followUp() therefore returns what the graph should learn: where the cause refines THE DESIGN, amend the design so the next estimate starts from what was learned; where it refines THE PROCESS — a blocking defect fixed in passing — record it separately, because absorbing it into this design's scope hides it." ;
    pred:decided "ANYTHING ILLEGITIMATE GOES TO A HUMAN, NOT A COUNCIL. Contestable-but-legitimate increases route to the council (F102 multi-model corroboration) where a single reviewer's judgement is worth checking. But accepting work that does not belong to a design is an ACCOUNTABILITY decision rather than a technical one, and a model must not be the last word on it." ;
