kb:credential-boundary
    rdfs:label "Credential classification and secret-safe exports" ;
    pred:principle "A static client cannot keep an operator-wide secret. Runtime user-supplied credentials may be browser-persisted by explicit choice; real deployment credentials must never be compiled into a distributed bundle." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:settings-unified-integrations ;
    pred:relates-to kb:settings-polish ;
    pred:feature-id "F107.5" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:part-of kb:stabilization-trust-boundaries ;
    pred:has-status "scaffolded" ;
    pred:description "Give every setting a security classification and enforce it recursively at every boundary. The current safe-to-share profile serializes nested Turtle/Hume credentials, while build-time VITE provider keys become public bundle defaults. Profiles, backups, logs, workspace files and production bundles need positive allowlists and sentinel-secret tests, not comments or TypeScript interfaces that disappear at runtime." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:integration-plugin-sdk ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:remaining "DONE WHEN every settings field is classified secret/sensitive/public; recursive schema-driven redaction covers every export, backup, log and workspace-profile path; sentinel-secret tests prove nested credentials cannot escape; a build guard rejects real provider secrets in app and extension bundles; legacy credentials migrate safely; and UI/docs state where each credential lives, where it is sent, and what a static client cannot protect." ;
    pred:progress "DONE 2026-07-22 (core leak + build guard). THE LEAK: the 'safe to share' settings profile allowlisted top-level fields but embedded turtleSettings whole, and turtleSettings carries humeApiKey + humeSecretKey — so a key escaped a 'no secrets' export. FIX: src/lib/safety/redact.ts recursively drops any secret-NAMED field at any depth (positive rule, not a denylist that new nested creds would slip past); buildSettingsProfileJson runs it as a final pass. A sentinel test (settings-profile-secrets.test.ts) seeds top-level AND nested-in-turtleSettings sentinels and proves neither appears in the serialized profile, while public fields (models, humeConfigId) survive. BUILD GUARD: scripts/offline/secret-scan.ts (npm run secret:scan, now in CI check job) fails if any secret-named VITE_ var referenced in source (10 found: VITE_*_API_KEY, VITE_HUME_SECRET_KEY) is set in the build env — a prod build would inline it into the public bundle — and scans any build/ output for set secret values as a backstop. STILL OPEN: an explicit per-field secret/sensitive/public classification map; extending recursive redaction to the OTHER boundaries (full KB backup, logs, workspace-profile writes); safe legacy-credential migration; and UI/docs stating where each credential lives, where it is sent, and what a static client cannot protect." ;
    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:relates-to kb:data-egress-model .

