    pred:progress "VISUAL/E2E FOLLOW-UP 2026-08-16 (uncommitted): scoped local agents found a fullscreen Escape propagation regression and notification-bell stacking collision introduced/exposed by the accessibility maintenance. Fullscreen now stops Escape propagation so it steps back to large, and sits above the notification bell. Focused Chromium preview flow was extended to prove focus entry, Escape, backdrop and explicit close; it completed without a Playwright error artifact. Jcode is not installed; retain only compact evidence capsules for local agents. Full device verification remains incomplete because this host's WebKit lacks libavif16; do not count those launch failures as application evidence." ;
    pred:progress "MAINTENANCE SLICE 2026-08-16 (uncommitted): Svelte check moved from 0 errors / 81 warnings in 21 files to 0 errors / 4 warnings in 2 files, without suppression. Repaired the calendar's invalid nested button with a keyboard-operable event shell; corrected popup/menu/group labels and state-selection semantics; associated input labels; replaced deprecated handlers; made the merge backdrop dismiss only on an actual backdrop click; removed compiler-confirmed dead CSS; corrected reactive references, stale edit drafts and explicit initial state; and replaced static autofocus with a client-only focus-on-mount action for intentional edit/dialog focus. Asset thumbnails and fullscreen image/3D paths now use named native or keyboard-operable controls, and fullscreen is a labelled backdrop-bounded dialog. Full suite remains 146 files / 2,016 tests and production build passes. Four remaining warnings have a deliberate next step: define Sheet swipe keyboard semantics; relocate/structure non-control graph pointer observation; and model real video caption-track URLs for both viewer renderings. No empty caption track or warning suppression was added." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:mobile-uiux ;
    pred:constraint "Do not treat the current raw sub-44px count as a pass/fail total: it includes noninteractive and intentionally compact elements. First repair audit classification, then ratchet verified interactive violations to zero without inflating visual density indiscriminately." ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:description "Turn the existing UI rubric and compiler diagnostics into a blocking interaction contract. Interactive controls need sufficient target size and visible focus; small semantic text needs a contrast-safe token rather than the decorative purple data color; dialogs, menus, disclosures, dividers, graph controls, and mobile sheets must be operable by keyboard and coarse pointer; labels must name controls; and motion/media need appropriate alternatives. Deterministic audits identify candidates, while focused semantic tests and human visual review decide whether each candidate is a real defect." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:deep-testing ;
