    pred:remaining "DONE WHEN token-level contrast tests cover text roles; verified interactive targets meet the chosen mobile target-size standard or carry a documented exception; every primary workflow is keyboard-completable with visible focus; touch-only and pointer-only controls have equivalents; labels, roles, dialog focus management, dividers, motion preferences and media alternatives pass automated and manual checks; Svelte accessibility warnings are ratcheted to zero; and the corrected device audit reports no unexplained target, overlap, clipping, or focus violations on supported routes." .

kb:node-synonyms
    rdfs:label "Phase 2 — user-managed synonyms on each node (skos:altLabel)" ;
    pred:constraint "PER-NODE IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN, and the gap is already live in this project. Entity-specific aliases ('entity set' = 'group' = 'batch') belong on the node. GLOBAL vocabulary equivalences do not: the KB -> graph terminology migration means 'graph' = 'KB' = 'knowledge base' across essentially every entity, and writing that onto 1,789 nodes is absurd. So a graph-level synonym set is needed as well. Build per-node FIRST (it is the one the user will actually maintain), and treat the global set as a second tier rather than pretending one mechanism covers both." ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Phase> ;
    pred:remaining "Not built. altLabel editing in the node panel; BM25 query expansion over altLabels with match attribution; alias-collision -> merge suggestion; embedding-proposed aliases as pending facts; graph-level synonym set as the second tier." ;
    pred:constraint "AN ALIAS COLLISION IS A DUPLICATE SIGNAL, NOT A CONFLICT TO RESOLVE SILENTLY. If two entities claim the same altLabel they are probably the same thing — which is exactly what kb:entity-normalization already detects by embedding similarity. Route collisions into the existing merge-suggestion path rather than letting search quietly return both and calling it recall." ;
    pred:principle "PUT THE VOCABULARY WHERE THE USER ALREADY IS (Matt, 2026-07-19: 'user managed synonyms on each node might be good'). A synonym added while looking at the node costs nothing; the same synonym added in a separate taxonomy manager costs a context switch, and will therefore not be added. This is kb:loop-idea-inbox's rule applied to vocabulary — capture must cost nothing or it will not happen — and it is why per-node aliases beat a standalone thesaurus tool for the first cut, even though the standalone tool is more powerful." ;
    pred:part-of kb:search-consistency ;
    pred:description "Each entity may carry skos:altLabel values the user writes, and BM25 expands queries across them. Standards-native, not a custom field: the graph is ALREADY SKOS (skos:definition 517 uses, skos:broader 420), while altLabel/prefLabel/hiddenLabel are used ZERO times and nothing in src/ or mcp-server/ reads them — so this activates an unused half of a standard already in play, and it round-trips in TTL and exports to any SKOS tool for free. UI home is obvious: the node detail panel already does inline label editing (saveLabel, src/routes/(app)/+page.svelte:1409), so aliases sit beside the label rather than in a new surface." ;
    pred:constraint "ALIASES ARE FACTS. They carry provenance and review status like any other statement, so an embedding-PROPOSED alias (normalizeEntities already computes the similarity) lands as PENDING for review and is never auto-applied. A vocabulary the user did not agree to is not user-managed." ;
    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:honest-note "Synonyms trade PRECISION for recall, and the cost is not zero: expanding 'set' to 'group' will surface rows the user did not want. So the result must show WHICH ALIAS MATCHED — unexplained recall is no better than unexplained silence, and it is worse in one way, because it looks like it worked. Also note per-node aliases would NOT have caught the F65/loop-job-grouping duplication on their own unless someone had already thought to add 'group' to the set entity; embeddings (phase 3) are what catch the synonym nobody anticipated." .

