kb:loop-idea-inbox
    rdfs:label "Phase 1 — ideas are a GRAPH, diffed against the roadmap" ;
    pred:principle "An idea graph is the mission in miniature: it is mostly well-formed absences. Subject and predicate known, object open. The orchestrator's job is to ask about the objects — not to invent them." ;
    pred:remaining "A low-friction capture surface (chat, CLI, voice) writing to an `ideas` graph; scheduled diff of ideas -> roadmap; conflicts surfaced as questions the orchestrator asks; accepted ideas promoted into the roadmap as planned features (a USER-AUTHORITY act, per F88 — minting a feature is authorship, not observation)." ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Phase> ;
    pred:description "Matt: 'ideas could be a separate graph and diff against roadmap'. That is the right shape, and it is better than an inbox — because it REUSES THE PRODUCT instead of inventing a sidecar. Ideas land in their own graph with no structure demanded at capture. Diffing that graph against the roadmap then answers, for free, the three questions that matter: what here is NEW, what REINFORCES something already planned, and what CONFLICTS with something we have already decided. That third one is the payoff, and an inbox could never give it: 'this idea contradicts a principle you hold' is precisely the thing you want said back to you, and precisely the thing a list of notes cannot say." ;
    pred:principle "CAPTURE MUST COST NOTHING OR IT WILL NOT HAPPEN. Friction at the moment of the idea — a required field, a type, a parent — trades the idea for the metadata, and the idea was the valuable half. The structure is recovered later, by DIFFING, not demanded up front." ;
    pred:reuses "The machinery already exists and is shipped: multi-graph registry, importAsNewKb, computeDiff/semanticDiff (new · reinforces · conflicts · refines), cross-graph align (F16), and the MergeReview UI. An idea graph is just another graph, which is the whole point." ;
    pred:part-of kb:autonomous-loop ;
    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "1"^^xsd:integer .

kb:local-session-memory
    pred:depends-on kb:context-compression ;
    pred:decided "RETRIEVAL PACK. Query confirmed graph facts first, then retrieve relevant archived human turns under separate token budgets. Every item is labelled graph or session, with source id, age and revision/supersession state. Empty/unreachable memory fails open to an empty pack; low retrieval confidence is disclosed, and absence from the pack is never presented as absence from the graph or history." ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/integrations/llm/turtle-chat.ts" ;
    pred:decided "PROMOTION FLOW. A candidate durable judgement is extracted into a pending Statement/GraphPatch carrying the originating event anchors. The user may accept, refine or reject it. Acceptance links the fact to the session source but does not delete or rewrite the turn; rejection teaches proposal yield without making the underlying private archive part of the graph." ;
    pred:depends-on kb:control-model ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:remaining "DONE WHEN Shelly and one coding-agent adapter write the same event format; a new session receives a bounded pack containing a known prior correction; a superseded turn is labelled stale rather than current; memory unavailable never blocks the host; promotion creates a pending fact with event provenance; and disabling/deleting memory leaves the authoritative graph intact." ;
    pred:part-of kb:context-engine ;
    pred:description "Add an opt-in local source archive for Shelly, Claude Code and Codex sessions, then retrieve a small request-specific context pack. The archive preserves what was said; the graph preserves what was accepted. A remembered turn may inform or motivate a fact but never becomes authoritative knowledge without the normal proposal/review boundary." ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:agent-context-dogfooding ;
    pred:relates-to kb:auto-archive ;
    pred:measurement "Measure retrieval recall against known prior decisions, false/stale recall, repeated-orientation-question rate, tokens injected versus displaced search, pack latency, storage growth and accepted-over-proposed promotion yield. Per-user live counters are required; a global token-savings claim is not evidence of value for this user's archive." ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:touches-file "mcp-server/src/index.ts" ;
    rdfs:label "Optional local session memory — archive turns, retrieve packs, promote judgement" ;
    pred:feature-id "F135.3" ;
    pred:decided "EVENT CONTRACT. Host adapters append a neutral SessionEvent with eventId, sessionId, harness, role, timestamp, parent/sequence, exact text or tool-result reference, content hash and optional supersedes link. Human turns remain verbatim and immutable as F135 decided; a correction appends a new event. Assistant/tool material is separately configurable and retention-bounded because it dominates volume and is largely re-derivable." ;
    pred:decided "PRIVACY BOUNDARY. Session capture is off until the user enables it for an explicit private location. It is device/workspace-local, excluded from graph sync and publication by default, has inspect/delete/export controls and never records provider keys or environment secrets. Sharing a graph cannot silently share the conversation that produced it." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:extraction-run-ledger .

