    pred:has-file "mcp-server/src/merge.ts" ;
    pred:description "A sub-agent does not return a chat summary; it returns a GRAPH — its findings, its claims, and its open questions, in its own namespace. Opus then merges those graphs into the trunk. This is the sharpest possible dogfooding: merging independent graphs, with provenance and a review status per fact, is the product. The primitives already exist (multi-graph registry, importAsNewKb, cross-graph align F16, MergeReview UI); what is missing is an MCP tool so an ORCHESTRATOR can drive the merge, not just a human clicking." ;
    pred:principle "A sub-agent's output is a CLAIM, not a fact. It arrives as pending, in its own graph, and becomes trunk only by passing a competent gate. An agent that can write directly to the trunk is not a sub-agent, it is an unreviewed committer." ;
    rdfs:label "Phase 2 — sub-agents write their own graphs; Opus merges" .

