kb:feedback-channel
    pred:remaining "Capture into a dedicated FEEDBACK GRAPH with provenance (see the ideas graph, idea:feedback-graph) so feedback and the ideas graph feed the roadmap through a reviewed merge rather than a maintainer reading an inbox. Also: the source label is a coarse route only ('review', 'kb') — deliberately, since a full path can carry private graph names, but it means a report cannot yet be tied to the specific state that caused it." ;
    pred:honest-note "PROVEN end to end 2026-07-23: a live submission through the production webhook sent an email via Graph (execution 1131, node returned success, mail received). The delivery is over the MICROSOFT GRAPH API, not SMTP — SMTP is a dead end on this M365 tenant because Security Defaults block Basic-Auth SMTP AUTH (535 5.7.139); Graph over HTTPS works under Security Defaults. Whether it is CONNECTED in production is still a BUILD-TIME setting (VITE_FEEDBACK_WEBHOOK_URL in Cloudflare Pages) that the code cannot assert — UNSET AS OF 2026-07-23, so the LIVE site still falls back to mailto until that env var is set and redeployed. The webhook is PUBLIC and UNAUTHENTICATED: the workflow drops empty and oversized messages and keeps CR/LF out of mail headers, but nothing rate-limits it and the app sends no shared secret." ;
    pred:has-status "functional" ;
    pred:scope-decision "The feedback endpoint is PRODUCT config, NOT the user's own n8n (settings.n8nBaseUrl). It briefly was the latter, which silently lost feedback from anyone running their own n8n: the POST went to THEIR server, which has no reckons-contact workflow, 404ed, and the maintainers never saw it — hitting exactly the technical users most likely to have something worth saying. Every OTHER n8n feature (currents sync, review notifications) correctly uses the user's instance, because those fire into the user's systems. Feedback travels the other way." ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/integrations/n8n/__tests__/contact.test.ts" ;
    pred:description "Feedback form reachable from every page (nav pencil, opens in place) and on /about (ContactForm.svelte). It POSTs to a build-time PRODUCT endpoint (VITE_FEEDBACK_WEBHOOK_URL); when that is unset it degrades to a mailto link to matthew.roe@data-insight.solutions. An importable n8n workflow (static/n8n/contact-feedback.workflow.json) validates/sanitizes the submission and sends it to email via the MICROSOFT GRAPH API (OAuth2), with Reply-To set to the submitter." ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/integrations/n8n/__tests__/contact-workflow.test.ts" ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/n8n> ;
    rdfs:label "Feedback channel (suggestion box)" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> .

kb:question-context-pages
    pred:relates-to kb:partial-facts ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:depends-on kb:graph-publishing ;
    pred:description "An OPTIONAL short context/summary page attached to a specific pending triple or '? question' fact, to give the reviewer what they need to decide. MOTIVATION: the Review tab surfaces partial facts needing an answer (F32 — incoming.needsObject, the 'questions only' filter in routes/(app)/review/+page.svelte), but a bare subject-predicate-? is often not enough context to accept/answer/reject confidently. DESIGN (reuses F27 + F44): the page is a WebPage-like node authored in Sveltia (content/*.md <-> graph round-trip), linked to the question via kpred:context-for -> [the statement/question id or subject IRI], rendered inline in the review card as an expandable summary (excerpt in graph, long-form in the .md). Content can be human-written OR drafted by Shelly grounded in the graph (kb_generate_page / kb_entity_markdown / kb_compress) then edited. Distinct from the answer itself (knowledge.answers.jsonl) — this is decision-support context, not the decision. Kept optional and lightweight so most questions need none. More urgent than F44's change-note use because it unblocks review throughput directly. Relates to F32 partial facts, F44 change notes, and F27 publishing." ;
    rdfs:label "Triple-Question Context Pages" ;
