    pred:known-issue "THE FIRST REAL CALLER FOUND A BUG THAT GREEN TESTS HAD HIDDEN FOR WEEKS. toTriG pushed opts.header RAW instead of as a comment, so any caller passing one produced invalid TriG — 'Unexpected full on line 1'. toTurtle and toTurtleFull both comment theirs; toTriG was the odd one out. Every existing test called toTriG() with NO header, so the function sat behind full coverage while being broken for the exact shape its first caller used. Caught by driving the actual UI and parsing the downloaded bytes, not by a unit test — the F55 lesson again, in a new place. Fixed, with three regression tests including one asserting toTriG and toTurtle agree on header handling." ;
    pred:remaining "DONE: toTriG wired into the export UI and verified end to end. DECLINED WITH EVIDENCE: per-file .trig adoption (no local graph carries >1 source). STILL OPEN: whether a pure-text multi-KB meta-file is wanted enough to overload the graph term — unchanged, and still nobody's call but Matt's." ;
