kb:ttl-trig-split
    pred:principle "PROVENANCE IS AN ACCOUNTABILITY RELATION, NOT A FIELD. It requires a party who can be held to it. A source the user controls and can rewrite is an attestation, not evidence." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:data-egress-model ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Concept> ;
    pred:principle "PUBLISHING IS THE MOMENT A GRAPH ACQUIRES AN OWNER, AND THEREFORE ACQUIRES PROVENANCE. Not manual file-sharing — handing someone a .ttl transfers no accountability. Official publication attributes the graph to a person or org who can be held to it." ;
    pred:description "TTL is the PRIVATE side: offline-capable, plain-text, fully under the user's control, no accountability and none required. TriG is the PUBLISHED side: named graphs carry an attributed, accountable publication context, which is what makes provenance mean anything. The two are not competing serializations — they are the individual product and the institutional one." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:adult-content-policy ;
    pred:part-of kb:reckons-ai ;
    pred:principle "A PRIVATE GRAPH HAS NO PROVENANCE, AND DOES NOT NEED ANY. It is the user's own reasoning, on the user's own device. He is the authority, and that is fine — because he is the only audience. Provenance is a claim made TO SOMEONE ELSE." ;
    rdfs:label "The TTL / TriG split — private power vs published accountability" .

