kb:predicate-appearance-inheritance
    pred:constraint "A COLLAPSED SET DOES NOT INHERIT ONE MEMBER'S STATUS BY ACCIDENT. Member-to-set propagation is off by default and requires an explicit aggregation policy such as all, majority, highest-priority or mixed, with a provenance trace and a visible mixed state." ;
    pred:estimated-files "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:touches-file "src/routes/(app)/+page.svelte" ;
    pred:estimated-deps "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:constraint "MVP IS ONE HOP. Later recursion uses a visited (node, rule) set, maximum depth three and per-hop attenuation; cycles terminate and output is invariant under statement order. Accepted extractor confidence does not multiply visual strength. Invalid enum, range or dangling references produce diagnostics and no rule, never a renderer crash." ;
    pred:honest-note "PLANNED, NO EXISTING FEATURE COVERS THIS (audited 2026-08-17). Predicate Manager currently counts, renames and merges predicates only. 2D hard-codes edge colors, 3D uses one global line material, and both renderers reduce predicates to local slugs so two namespaces can collide. Presentation predicates are excluded before renderer props, so the resolver must receive full confirmed statements or an upstream appearance map rather than being hidden inside a renderer." ;
    pred:depends-on kb:predicate-manager ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/3d/KnowledgeGraph.svelte" ;
    pred:phase "P0 CONTRACT: pure RDF parser/validator plus shared base/entity/node/edge resolver, diagnostics, provenance traces, literal and IRI fixtures, deterministic conflict/cycle tests, graph-lint rules for invalid configuration and a 1k/10k O(V + E + R) benchmark." ;
    pred:decided "DIRECT EDGE STYLE AND PROPAGATION ARE DIFFERENT DATA. A predicate appearance definition may carry edge color, opacity, width, dash and label treatment. Each propagation is a separate ktype:VisualStyleRule entity so one predicate can express several rules: full predicate IRI, direction, source mode (endpoint appearance or fixed), source attribute/value/type, target type, target channel (fill, outline, glow, icon, opacity), strength 0..1, priority, enabled, scope, max depth, attenuation and conflict policy." ;
    pred:decided "DETERMINISTIC CASCADE: explicit entity appearance > predicate inheritance contributions ordered by priority then stable rule/source key > explicitly configured set aggregation > entity type > fallback. Strength blends color over the lower semantic base in sRGB and interpolates scalar channels; non-blendable icon/shape uses the winning rule. Equal-priority disagreement emits a conflict trace and deterministic configured outcome; blend is opt-in, never accidental `find()` or last-write behavior." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:feature-lifecycle-vocab ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/components/PredicateManager.svelte" ;
    pred:feature-id "F138" ;
    pred:principle "CONFIRMED FACTS DRIVE CANONICAL APPEARANCE. Confirmed/refined relationships may contribute; rejected and superseded never do. A pending relationship may preview through a dashed or provisional halo with explicit provenance, but must not silently turn the canonical fill green." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:graph-legibility ;
    pred:principle "VISUAL PROVENANCE IS PART OF THE RESULT. The resolver returns rule, relation statement, source term, strength and any suppressed conflict so the inspector can say 'green via has-status from Published (100%)'. Derived appearance is view state and is never written back as kpred:color or multiplied into export." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:one-graph-canvas ;
    rdfs:label "Predicate appearance and visual inheritance" ;
    pred:principle "STATUS CANNOT BE ENCODED ONLY BY HUE. Rules may pair fill with outline, icon, dash or label; contrast and non-color channels are acceptance criteria. A source/hub layout that owns fill must preserve semantic status in a secondary channel or disclose the masking in the legend." ;
    pred:acceptance "Rejected/superseded facts never contribute; pending does not alter canonical fill; equal-priority conflict is visible; cycles terminate; invalid rules diagnose; same local slug in two vocabularies styles separately; config entities never enter the scene; export/import round-trips rule RDF; 2D and 3D use the same resolved map and preserve a non-color status channel." ;
    pred:phase "P1 EDITOR: Predicate Manager appearance editor, direct edge style, one-hop color inheritance and provenance legend. P2 RENDER: one full-IRI scene map drives 2D and 3D; 3D vertex colors ship before renderer-specific width/dash work; pending preview and export/import get end-to-end coverage. P3 adds bounded recursion, literal palettes and explicit set/multi-graph scopes." ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/rdf/predicate-appearance.ts" ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:description "Let a predicate define its own edge appearance and one or more first-class visual inheritance rules, so a relation such as Article has-status Published can make the article visibly production-green with an explainable trace. Predicate Manager gains a customization surface parallel to Entity Types without materializing the derived appearance as a fact on every related node." ;
    pred:decided "SUPPORT BOTH STATUS SHAPES. Endpoint appearance handles an IRI object such as a green Published node. A value-conditioned fixed rule handles today's free-text status literal such as `production`, so this feature is not blocked on F75.2's planned SKOS migration. External predicates can be styled by full IRI without renaming them." ;
    pred:acceptance "Published has explicit #22c55e; Article has-status Published plus object-to-subject color rule resolves Article green with a trace, and removing the relation restores its type color. The equivalent literal `production` fixture resolves green. Strength 0/0.5/1 is exact; explicit entity wins; inherited beats type; priority and shuffled statement order are deterministic." ;
    pred:depends-on kb:entity-appearance-resolver ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:set-view ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/3d/KnowledgeGraph2D.svelte" .

