kb:scope-estimate-derivation
    pred:description "Matt, 2026-08-14: 'shouldn't the code graph have detailed connections for concepts, across multiple files? I see that as a source for the estimates, not just a random guess.' A new edge, kpred:touches-module, links a DESIGN to the code concepts it expects to work in, so an estimate can be bounded by what those modules actually contain." ;
    rdfs:label "Estimates derived from the code graph, not guessed" ;
    pred:part-of kb:scope-creep ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/scope-derive.test.ts" ;
    pred:principle "DERIVATION HONESTLY GIVES A BOUND, NOT A NUMBER. A module is not a file: naming code:rdf names 24 files and a feature will touch some of them. So the graph yields an UPPER BOUND (every file in every named module) and, where specific files are named, a LOWER BOUND. The estimate lies between — and an estimate ABOVE the upper bound is a contradiction the graph can catch, because you cannot touch more files than exist in the modules you named. The interesting reading of that failure is not 'the number is too big' but 'the design has not named everywhere it will actually go'." ;
    pred:evidence "FIRST REAL RUN, F122 on its own branch: 2 modules named (code:rdf, code:stores), upper bound 46 files, graph suggestion ~14, hand-written estimate 6 — within bounds but well under what the modules imply. That gap is the useful output: either phase 2 is genuinely narrow or the estimate was optimistic, and now there is something to argue with rather than a bare number." ;
    pred:measured "THE EDGE WAS MISSING ENTIRELY, WHICH IS WHY THE FIRST ESTIMATES WERE GUESSES. Measured 2026-08-14: static/reckons-codebase.ttl carries exactly TWO predicates — kpred:has-file (379) and kpred:tested-by (44) — across 38 module concepts joined by skos:broader, and links to NOTHING in the roadmap. 'Which files will F122 touch' had no answer in the graph, so the numbers written for F122, F123 and F75 were invented." ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    pred:has-status "functional" ;
    pred:remaining "BUILT: kpred:touches-module on three designs, src/lib/rdf/scope-derive.ts (deriveScope, checkEstimate, suggestEstimate) wired into scope-check so every estimate is reported with its derived bound or flagged as an unbounded GUESS. NOT BUILT: only 3 of ~130 designs name their modules, so the other estimates remain underivable; and the codebase graph still has no concept-to-concept edges beyond skos:broader, so a design cannot yet be linked to a CONCEPT that spans modules — which is the richer version of what Matt asked for." ;
    pred:feature-id "F130.2" ;
    pred:constraint "THE SUGGESTED FRACTION IS A STATED CONVENTION, NOT A MEASUREMENT. suggestEstimate uses 30% of the module universe because a feature rarely touches every file in a module — but with zero designs yet carrying both an estimate and an actual there is nothing to calibrate it against, and presenting it as evidence would dress a convention up as data." .

