kb:browser-fact-finding
    pred:relates-to kb:entity-normalization ;
    pred:relates-to kb:browser-extension ;
    pred:description "Research in the browser, grounded in what you already know. (1) HIGHLIGHT: key statements on the page are marked as candidate facts — a passage, not a vibe, so every proposed triple keeps its excerpt and is verifiable against the page (kb:passage-grounding). (2) DEEP ANALYSIS ON DEMAND: the user asks, and only then does the expensive pass run — never a background crawl of everything they read. (3) LINK TO WHAT WE KNOW: query the graph with the page's key terms AND its content, surface the entities that genuinely overlap, and offer to connect the new facts to them." ;
