    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:feature-id "F107.1" ;
    pred:description "Close the MCP's local-code-execution boundary and make reader failure explicit. Replace shell-string child processes with argument-vector APIs; validate Git refs and tool arguments at runtime; audit every process-spawning path; distinguish invalid, empty, stale, and deleted graphs; and reconcile vanished readers instead of serving plausible old facts. MCP is local, but an LLM-controlled tool argument is still untrusted input." ;
    rdfs:label "MCP process execution containment and protocol health" ;
    pred:progress "COMPLETE 2026-07-22. (1) Command execution: git-utils.ts (the only process-spawning file, repo-wide grep exec|spawn) uses execFileSync('git', args[]) with no shell, sanitizeRef() rejecting leading-dash option-injection + non-revision characters, and a '--' terminator; the live injection via kb_git_diff_triples/kb_alignment_score ('ref: HEAD; <cmd>') is closed. (2) Runtime arg schemas: validate-args.ts validates every tools/call against the tool's own inputSchema (required present + non-empty, types match) and returns -32602 before any handler runs. (3) Reader health: kb-reader.ts distinguishes ok/empty/parse-error/missing — a corrupt file keeps last-good data but is flagged stale, a deleted graph drops its triples, and a vanished KB is reconciled out of the reader map instead of serving old facts; kb_stats/kb_list_kbs surface it. (4) The full MCP suite (build + vitest + node --test, 73+10 tests incl. adversarial injection, arg-validation, and health cases) now runs as a required CI job (.github/workflows/ci.yml `mcp`)." ;
    pred:has-status "functional" ;
    pred:constraint "The Git-diff/alignment tools were NOT actually disabled — they were live and injectable. As of 2026-07-22 hostile-ref tests prove shell metacharacters, newlines, command substitutions, and option-like refs cannot execute or reshape a command; that gate is now met. It stays met: any new process-spawning path must land with the same argument-vector + validation + adversarial-test discipline before it ships." ;
    pred:remaining "DONE WHEN every MCP child process uses execFile/spawn-style argument arrays with no shell interpolation; refs are validated and separated from options; runtime schemas reject malformed tool arguments; parse/deletion health is surfaced to callers; repository-wide process audit and adversarial injection tests block regressions; and the full MCP test suite runs as a required CI job." ;
