kb:mission
    pred:relates-to kb:async-orchestration ;
    pred:principle "A fact without its evidence — its excerpt, its diagram, its measurement — is a conclusion. It cannot be checked by anyone who was not there, which is everyone who matters." ;
    pred:principle "You cannot ask a question you have not discovered you have. The value of a partial fact is that it turns 'go find out what we are missing' into 'answer this one question, and four blocked things unblock'." ;
    pred:description "It is never about the tool. It is about the knowledge — and specifically about the knowledge you need to DECIDE, which is usually a few team members away. That is a distance problem, not an information problem." ;
    pred:principle "Detection is an arms race; provenance is durable. Every forensic tell you publish becomes a term in the next model's objective. Attribution to an accountable party does not get outrun by better generators, because it was never about how convincing the artifact is." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:thesis ;
    pred:principle "A document records CONCLUSIONS, not the structure that produced them. Two documents cannot be diffed for reasoning; two graphs can." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Concept> ;
    rdfs:label "The mission" ;
    pred:principle "THE INVENTION IS NOT WHAT THE GRAPH STORES. It is that the graph can hold the SHAPE OF WHAT IS MISSING. A well-formed absence — subject and predicate known, object unknown, and here is what it blocks — is the most useful node in the graph." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:partial-facts ;
    pred:principle "The most decision-relevant knowledge is the stuff nobody wrote down, held by someone who does not know it is load-bearing. A graph CANNOT extract what nobody thought to say — and claiming otherwise would be its own overclaim." ;
    pred:part-of kb:reckons-ai .

