kb:source-validation
    pred:relates-to kb:tenet-evidence ;
    pred:description "The thesis, made operational: an unverifiable claim, made by the party it benefits, is not evidence — so take a fact the graph asserts, SEARCH THE WEB for INDEPENDENT sources, and judge each as supporting, contradicting, or neither. Two outcomes matter and the second is the rare, valuable one: CORROBORATION (an outside source agrees → the fact earns provenance it never had) and CONFLICT (an outside source DISAGREES → the well-formed absence made visible, a contradiction the graph could not see from inside). Distinct from the enrichment pipeline, which ADDS facts from the web; this CHECKS facts already in the graph. Conflicts are NEVER auto-resolved — which source to believe is judgment, surfaced for review. src/lib/rdf/source-validation.ts is the deterministic harness (buildValidationQuery + verdictFromJudgments + validateFact); the two judgment plugins are injected: WHERE to search (tavily.ts, already in-repo) and WHETHER a source supports/contradicts (an LLM/NLI call, re-analyze.ts pattern). Runs in CI on mocks; provider-agnostic." ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/source-validation.test.ts" ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
    rdfs:label "Source validation — check a fact against the open web" ;
    pred:has-status "scaffolded" ;
    pred:decided "Matt (2026-07-16): yes — validate graph information against new sources, and flag CONFLICTING sources. Delivery = a per-graph SETTING (validate on/off) AND an optional POD MODE that validates facts in the background over time (like currents), so a graph can be continuously checked, not just on demand. Corroboration and conflict both emit as PROPOSALS for review — corroboration → a sourced suggestion; conflict → a drift-warning — never a silent write." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:enrichment-pipeline ;
    pred:feature-id "F100" ;
    pred:has-file "src/lib/rdf/source-validation.ts" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:remaining "Wire the harness to live plugins: search=tavily (settings key), judge=LLM (ETHICS_PREAMBLE injected). Emit results to knowledge.pending.jsonl — corroboration as a suggestion carrying the source URL as provenance; conflict as a drift-warning naming the disagreeing source. Review-tab surface (a 'validate' action per fact + a results view). Pod/background mode reusing the currents scheduler. Rate/cost guard (web search is metered)." .

