kb:loop-safety
    pred:evidence "TWO EXTERNAL CONFIRMATIONS OF THE TIERING DOCTRINE (repo scan, 2026-08-13). deerwork-ai/deer-workflow (470 stars, MIT) calls it Graph Engineering: control flow, phases, inputs and failure handling live in reviewable TypeScript while agents do only semantic work inside nodes — the same claim as ground/prompt/validate/emit-proposal, stated as an architecture with pluggable agent runtimes. plasma-ai/fractal (691 stars, Apache-2.0) contributes the concrete cap set this roadmap lacks: hard limits on iterations, DEPTH, children, cost AND wall-clock time, with per-node git worktree isolation (zero roadmap mentions of worktree). F124 currently plans a spend ceiling only. fractal also documents its own anti-pattern honestly — its nodes run without permission prompts by default — which is the failure mode kb:loop-safety exists to refuse." ;
    pred:description "A loop that fails silently at 3am is worse than no loop, because you will trust it. The known failure modes, each of which has already bitten this project once: (1) THE RUNNER DIED — a cron fired exactly on schedule, produced nothing, reported nothing, and still displayed a future run time. (2) THE HARNESS RAN OUT OF BUDGET — Opus hits a usage limit mid-orchestration and the task is 'in progress' forever; leases (F87 phase 3) hand it back. (3) DOUBLE ASSIGNMENT — two woken orchestrators take the same task; claims fix it. (4) THE TOOL WAS WRONG — published-graph-guard reported 166 phantom violations and kept a real gate switched off for a day. (5) THE AGENT REVIEWED NOTHING — a cold model load failed and the code review reported a clean run having read zero files." ;
    pred:remaining "Run outcomes as facts; lease expiry sweep; a rollback path for a merge that lands broken on main (production deploys from main)." ;
    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    pred:principle "SILENCE MUST NEVER LOOK LIKE SUCCESS. Every run writes its outcome back, including 'I did nothing, and here is why'. A green log that is always green is not a record." ;
    rdfs:label "Phase 5 — the ways this loop fails silently" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Phase> ;
    pred:principle "A FINDING IS A CLAIM. A tool reporting a violation is a party with an interest in having found one. Verify the finding before acting on it — especially when acting on it means weakening a control." ;
    pred:part-of kb:autonomous-loop .

