    pred:progress "DELEGATED VOICE TOKEN shipped 2026-07-22 (PR #143) but was never described here — recording it now to close the drift. src/lib/integrations/hume/token.ts: planHumeAuth() picks, in order, mint-local (owner has apiKey+secretKey — a short-lived token is minted, no raw key on the wire), api-key, then token-url, then none. fetchHumeTokenFromUrl() fetches a SHORT-LIVED access token from an opt-in endpoint the sharer runs (https enforced except localhost; accepts accessToken/access_token/token; every failure wrapped so the caller can fall back rather than hang). TurtleSettings.humeTokenUrl carries it, and because it is an endpoint rather than a credential it survives redaction and travels with a shared persona. THE POINT: someone opening a shared story hears the voice WITHOUT configuring their own Hume, while the sharer's secret key never leaves their control and the delegation stays revocable and rate-limitable — unlike a leaked key." ;
