kb:ocr-provider-benchmark
    rdfs:label "OCR provider contract and benchmark — text, layout, rotation and geometry" ;
    pred:priority "medium" ;
    pred:decided "FIXTURE POLICY. Use synthetic documents targeted at rotation, columns, headers/footers, tables, handwriting, low contrast and scans plus a small licensed real-document set. Illegible ground truth is marked unknown, and handwriting truth requires two independent readings where practical, so a provider is never rewarded for confidently inventing text." ;
    pred:description "Put Tesseract.js, Ollama VLM, Mistral OCR and any future docTR sidecar behind one capability-declared adapter returning DocumentIR. Providers are compared on the same fixtures before routing changes. The browser path remains the default local baseline; docTR is a benchmark/optional sidecar candidate, not a presumed replacement." ;
    pred:decided "BENCHMARK DIMENSIONS. Score character/word error, reading order, region classification, bbox intersection-over-union, rotation/orientation, table structure, hallucinated text, runtime, peak memory, model/download size and data-egress class separately. Preserve per-fixture results and provider versions; never collapse them into one leaderboard number that hides a local/privacy or geometry tradeoff." ;
    pred:depends-on kb:document-evidence-anchors ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/integrations/parsers/local-ocr.ts" ;
    pred:decided "PROVIDER CONTRACT. An adapter declares locality, supported media, text, layout, rotation, table and bbox capabilities plus runtime requirements. It returns DocumentIR pages/blocks with provider/model/version and timing, or a typed failure. A provider without geometry returns no geometry; a markdown-only response is not mislabeled layout-aware." ;
    pred:remaining "DONE WHEN one benchmark command runs every available provider on the shared corpus and emits rerunnable per-dimension results; current Tesseract and Mistral adapters both return DocumentIR honestly; rotated/two-column/table failures are separately visible; and docTR earns an optional adapter only if measured accuracy or geometry materially exceeds the shipped paths at an acceptable installation/runtime cost." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:visual-testing ;
    pred:constraint "ROUTING IS EXPLICIT AND CAPABILITY-BASED. Offline image ingest may prefer Tesseract; PDF/layout grounding may offer another provider when configured. No local document is sent to a cloud OCR service merely because it scores higher, and no heavyweight sidecar is installed automatically. The user sees locality, expected capability and cost before egress." ;
    pred:feature-id "F70.2" ;
    pred:touches-file "src/lib/integrations/parsers/mistral-ocr.ts" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:work-tiering ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
