    pred:tenet-status "built" ;
    pred:part-of kb:thesis ;
    pred:tenet-body "You cannot ask a question you have not discovered you have. So a fact whose object is still unknown is not a gap in the graph — it is the point of it. Subject known, predicate known, object still open, and four things stalled behind it. That turns 'go find out what we are missing' into 'answer this one question'. The knowledge you need to decide is usually a few people away; the hard part was never reaching them, it was knowing what to ask." .

