kb:calendar-write
    pred:remaining "Design the write channel; intent parsing (person + time + duration) with the person resolved against graph entities rather than invented; free-slot search over the events already imported; a confirmation affordance in Shelly and in the review queue; write-back to the graph with provenance." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:n8n-cloud-sync ;
    pred:has-status "planned" ;
    pred:priority "high" ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:relates-to kb:int-indico ;
    pred:feature-id "F99.2" ;
    pred:description "The half of the assistant that CHANGES the world: 'schedule an appointment with Chelsey at 3pm next Tuesday'. Parse the intent, resolve the person against the graph, find a free slot, and create a real calendar event — then write the event back into the graph as a fact with provenance, so the graph and the calendar agree." ;
    pred:part-of kb:personal-assistant ;
    pred:open-question "Which write channel? (a) an n8n workflow holding the server-side credential, which matches the Integration Boundaries rule that n8n owns web SIDE-EFFECTS while the app stays local-first, and keeps a write credential out of the browser; (b) write to a calendar that HAS a real write API (Google Calendar, or Nextcloud CalDAV per F63) and leave Indico read-only; (c) an Indico plugin exposing a create endpoint — most work, least reuse. Leaning (a)." ;
    rdfs:label "Schedule an appointment (calendar WRITE)" ;
    pred:honest-note "NOT A WIRING JOB — THE WRITE PATH DOES NOT EXIST. Measured 2026-07-31: src/lib/integrations/indico/client.ts has fetchEvents/searchEvents/getEvent and NO create, and Indico's HTTP API is effectively read-only for events. The eight starter-graph events on the live server were created through `indico shell` ON THE SERVER, which is not something a browser can do. So this feature needs a write channel that does not yet exist, and choosing it is a design decision, not an implementation detail." ;
    pred:decided "A CALENDAR WRITE IS A REAL-WORLD SIDE EFFECT AND MUST BE CONFIRMED, never auto-committed from a voice command. Consistent with F52 (agents propose, humans settle): the assistant drafts the event, shows time/attendee/duration, and a human accepts. A misheard 'next Tuesday' that silently books a real meeting with a real person is exactly the failure the review queue exists to prevent." .

kb:view-suggestions
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:principle "A suggestion must be EARNED BY THE DATA. Silence is the correct and common answer — six of the nineteen tests assert that we say nothing." ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/view-suggestions.test.ts" ;
    pred:principle "At most ONE suggestion. A menu of five things to try is not help, it is homework — and it is how a helpful feature becomes one the user mutes." ;
    pred:description "Reads the REAL view context — the facts currently drawn, the entity types the user selected, the node count, the connectivity shape, the layout in use — and offers at most ONE warranted change. Rules fire only on evidence that genuinely exists: a timeline when the visible facts carry dates spanning real time (weighted higher when the user has selected event/calendar types); grouping by type when several kinds of thing are mixed; the hubs when the view is crowded AND hub-shaped; grouping by source when the facts came from several documents. Every suggestion carries its evidence, shown and not implied. Dismiss once and it never returns." ;
    pred:known-issue "FIXED 2026-07-12 — ViewAdjust.layout omitted 'timeline' and 'hierarchy' while KnowledgeGraph supported them, so SHELLY COULD NOT REQUEST A TIMELINE LAYOUT AT ALL: the single most obvious thing to offer someone staring at dated facts. A view-control API that cannot express the view is not an API. Now typed from the one GraphLayout union both sides share." ;
    pred:feature-id "F85" ;
    pred:part-of kb:graph-legibility ;
    pred:principle "Show the evidence, never imply it. 'Trust me' is not a reason." ;
    pred:has-status "functional" ;
    pred:has-file "src/lib/rdf/view-suggestions.ts" ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
