kb:serena-prior-art
    pred:open-question "Adopt as an MCP server alongside the reckons one, or borrow the idea and compute symbol edges ourselves for TypeScript only? Serena is a general agent toolkit and this project needs one narrow output — the symbols a change actually reaches — so a targeted tsserver query may be the smaller answer. Weighing that needs someone to try it; nothing here has." ;
    pred:evidence "IT IS THE PROPER VERSION OF WHAT F130.4 APPROXIMATES. Import parsing gives file-to-file edges and stops there; a language server gives symbol-to-symbol — which of the 154 dependents of types.ts actually reference the field that changed. That is the difference between 'this file is risky to touch' and 'these nine call sites are affected'." ;
    pred:link "https://github.com/oraios/serena" ;
    pred:honest-note "NOT INSTALLED, NOT TRIED. Read from its README on 2026-08-14 and recorded as prior art. Every claim above is the project's own description, not a verified capability." ;
