kb:partial-facts
    pred:feature-id "F32" ;
    pred:touches-module <urn:reckons:code/rdf> ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Feature> ;
    pred:known-issue "GUARDED: computeDiff must never structurally diff a partial fact. Diffing '?' against an existing object compares a HOLE to a VALUE and produces a bogus conflict or refinement — the user would be asked to adjudicate nonsense. Now covered by a test." ;
    pred:part-of kb:mission ;
    pred:has-status "functional" ;
    pred:principle "A question with a price gets answered; one without does not. Always state what it blocks." ;
    rdfs:label "Partial Facts & Answer-Flow-Back" ;
    pred:tested-by "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/partial-facts.test.ts" ;
    pred:has-file "src/lib/rdf/partial-facts.ts" ;
    pred:principle "A partial fact is not a gap in the model. IT IS THE POINT OF IT. You cannot ask a question you have not discovered you have (kb:mission)." ;
    pred:known-issue "FIXED 2026-07-13 — THE FEATURE THE MISSION RESTS ON HAD NO TESTS, and two fields were being DROPPED on import. (1) `blocks` was discarded, so the graph knew it had a hole but not what the hole COST — which is the difference between a to-do and a priority, and it is the entire 'answer this one question and four blocked things unblock' value. The landing page was already claiming it worked. (2) `askedBy` was discarded, so an answer came back unattributed and could not be claimed by the agent waiting on it — which breaks the moment more than one agent is running. Both now survive drainWorkspacePending; DiffEntry builds the answer via resolvePartial() so the wiring cannot silently rot again." ;
    pred:description "A triple whose object is unknown: subject and predicate asserted, object '?', needsObject true. The Review tab renders an entity picker instead of accept/reject; answering it writes back to knowledge.answers.jsonl where the agent that asked resumes. A question now also carries WHAT IT BLOCKS and WHO ASKED, so the graph can answer the question that matters — not 'what don't we know?' (a list of holes, demoralizing and unactionable) but 'what would answering THIS unblock?'. questionsByImpact ranks open questions by how much they free up, breaking ties toward the OLDER question, because a hole nobody has filled in a week is evidence nobody will fill it by accident." .

