kb:ref-nvidia-switchyard
    rdfs:label "NVIDIA NeMo Switchyard — multi-provider LLM routing proxy and library" ;
    pred:description "README reviewed 2026-08-16. A pre-alpha Rust proxy/library that translates OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses and Anthropic Messages traffic, selects among local and remote OpenAI-compatible targets, and exports request, error, latency, token and routing-overhead metrics. Its documented strategies include pass-through, random splits, an LLM classifier, deterministic conversation-stage routing and weak-first/judge/escalate routing." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:extraction-run-ledger ;
    pred:scope-decision "Copy the route-policy and observability contract into TypeScript first. Later, allow a user-configured localhost Switchyard endpoint/sidecar as one provider adapter if it beats the native router on measured reliability or operational simplicity; never require it for ordinary browser use." ;
    pred:relates-to kb:llm-providers ;
    pred:repo-url "https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Switchyard" ;
    pred:license "Apache-2.0" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:model-routing-ledger ;
    pred:constraint "PRE-ALPHA REFERENCE, NOT A CORE DEPENDENCY. An always-on native proxy conflicts with the shipped browser/static-host path, and a generic fallback can silently turn local processing into cloud egress. Protocol translation may also flatten provider-specific streaming, structured-output, tool-call or safety semantics. No adoption before conformance tests, explicit locality policy and visible per-attempt failure evidence." ;
    pred:evidence "STAGE ROUTING IS THE STRONGEST FIT. A known workflow signal — tool result, parse error, validator failure or stage marker — can select the next model tier without paying a classifier model or asking a model to grade itself. Its library boundary also demonstrates that route selection can return a target decision without owning the provider call, which fits Reckons' existing direct-browser adapters better than mandatory proxying." ;
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Reference> ;
    pred:relates-to kb:aggressive-local-offload ;
    pred:copy-permitted "yes — Apache-2.0: attribution + NOTICE, express patent grant" ;
    pred:relates-to kb:work-tiering .

